  "notes": [
    "Fix for guard fault: every guard now draws the one variant with preShift cafe and evening square (night variant removed), so both `at` ties (pre-shift, evening) can always be kept for the door guard.",
    "[S] Guard regular ties listed first in the row so the workmate pattern cannot use up the guard's tie slots; workmate ties restricted to clerk and guard, driver keeps the councillor tie.",
    "[S] Café row drops its own regular tie to servers: it took servers' tie capacity; the keeper learns needs from workmate ties.",
    "[S] Café fearful cut to 13%: Help does not turn a fearful server. Question for Motive: a per-position temperament list would keep fearful from server and driver.",
    "[S] Office: 1 door guard, 1 service door, rest inside at official side; watch count 2 takes the door at the chime. Councillor and driver 1 each, car, [0,0].",
    "[S] Square use stays small (guards' evening, 15% of café and kiosk, 20% of residents); chairs are the café's 48.",
    "[S] Kiosk rows are walk-only: the 05:00 shift would arrive before the first tram. Occupation ids follow row ids (diner); Motive to confirm."
